4. Binary star system 
 
Computers represent information in binary. 
 
Binary number (bits) 
 
A bit is the smallest unit of information in a computer. 
 
A bit can only have two possible values: 0 or 1. 
 
Key terms: 
 
Binary number 
 
One bit = a binary digit (0 or 1)
